.Dd March 12, 2026
.Dt KEYBOARD 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm keyboard
.Nd PS/2 keyboard input driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "device keyboard"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver handles IRQ1 input from the PS/2 keyboard path.
It reads translated Set 1 scancodes from port
.Li 0x60 ,
tracks modifier state, translates supported key presses into ASCII, and forwards
the resulting input to the active virtual terminal and the kernel input-event
stream.
.Pp
The current implementation supports:
.Bl -bullet
.It
single-byte Set 1 printable keys
.It
left and right Shift/Ctrl/Alt state tracking
.It
translation through the active keymap, including Ctrl-generated control bytes
.It
.Li Alt+Fn
virtual-terminal switching
.It
ANSI escape emission for extended cursor and navigation keys
.It
.Li Shift+PageUp
and
.Li Shift+PageDown
for VT scrollback navigation
.It
.Li Ctrl+F9
kernel process-table dump
.El
.Pp
Translated characters are queued in an internal ring buffer and forwarded to the
active VT's TTY. If no TTY is attached, input falls back to the console input
path. The driver also emits key press and key release notifications through the
generic input-event interface.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/sys/drivers/input/keyboard.c"
.It Pa /sys/drivers/input/keyboard.c
Driver implementation.
.It Pa /sys/drivers/input/keyboard.h
Driver interface.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ps2 4 ,
.Xr tty 4
